ble items, including the automation interpretation.\n- Verify that all schedule tasks' dates are weekdays (not weekends) and that Test Env A and UAT tasks lie within their windows. Verify the public holiday 2025-10-23 is not counted in duration_days.\n- Confirm assigned resources match availability (Charlie assigned only to tasks where his 50% capacity suffices; if automation_setup demands 12 hours, Charlie must be scheduled for 3 working days at 4h/day).\n- Confirm the totals in estimates do not exceed plausible capacity; for basic exam expect candidates to keep total estimated hours <= (Alice capacity + Bob capacity + Charlie available hours during test window) unless the candidate documents a justified adjustment.\n\nThis optional_attachments text intentionally contains both the per-field explanation and the pass/fail criteria so the evaluator has a single authoritative reference when scoring candidate submissions.",
